IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `scr-dates`
IMPORT `scr-duties`
IMPORT `scr-costs`

-- Supreme Court (General Civil Procedure) Rules 2025 (Vic) -- worked cases for the party's questions about security for
-- costs, costs, money in court and child abuse claims against unincorporated organisations (scr-costs.l4). Every expected
-- value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim
-- about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- Calendar used: 2 November 2026 is a Monday; 1 December 2026 a Tuesday; 1 January 2027 a Friday. The Christmas vacation
-- (24 December to 9 January) is 17 days.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

§§ `Order 62 -- security for costs`

-- Arguments: lives outside Victoria, sues for another without assets, other case pending, address missing or wrong,
-- innocent, changed address to avoid, an Act.
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Can my claim be dismissed for want of security` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my claim be dismissed for want of security` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my claim be dismissed for want of security` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Order 63 -- costs`

#ASSERT `Can I recover my costs` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I recover my costs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I recover my costs` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `Must I pay the costs of my extension application` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I pay the costs of my extension application` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Are these costs in the proceeding` `an amendment of a pleading` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are these costs in the proceeding` `an interlocutory application with no order, or an order silent on costs` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are these costs in the proceeding` `an application or step whose costs were reserved` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Must I pay the costs of proof` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I pay the costs of proof` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I pay the costs of proof` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `What can follow unpaid interlocutory costs` `the side making the claim` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `my proceeding may be stayed or dismissed`
#ASSERT `What can follow unpaid interlocutory costs` `the side the claim is against` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `my defence may be struck out`
#ASSERT `What can follow unpaid interlocutory costs` `the side making the claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What can follow unpaid interlocutory costs` `the side making the claim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `May I tax my interlocutory costs now` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I tax my interlocutory costs now` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I tax my interlocutory costs now` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `On what basis are my costs taxed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the standard basis: all costs reasonably incurred and of reasonable amount`
#ASSERT `On what basis are my costs taxed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the indemnity basis: all costs except those of unreasonable amount or unreasonably incurred, any doubt resolved in my favour`
#ASSERT `On what basis are my costs taxed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the basis the Court directed`

#ASSERT `Can my lawyer be made to pay the costs` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my lawyer be made to pay the costs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my lawyer be made to pay the costs` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Appendix A -- the scale`

-- Arguments: who, years since admission, work from 1 January 2026, increase per cent.
#ASSERT `What is the most per hour for this work` `a legal practitioner, doing legal work` 12 TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 918
#ASSERT `What is the most per hour for this work` `a legal practitioner, doing legal work` 10 TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 918
-- 9 years 6 months: 9 completed years, the 5 to 9 band (fork F16).
#ASSERT `What is the most per hour for this work` `a legal practitioner, doing legal work` 9.5 TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 663
#ASSERT `What is the most per hour for this work` `a legal practitioner, doing legal work` 5 TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 663
#ASSERT `What is the most per hour for this work` `a legal practitioner, doing legal work` 4.9 TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 459
#ASSERT `What is the most per hour for this work` `an employee who is not a legal practitioner, doing legal work` 0 TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 398
#ASSERT `What is the most per hour for this work` `an employee who is not a legal practitioner, doing clerical work` 0 TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 296
#ASSERT `What is the most per hour for this work` `a supporting professional (accountant, financial adviser, IT specialist, analyst)` 0 TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 677
-- With the full 30% increase: $918 x 1.3 = $1193.40; 10% on $398 = $437.80; 31% is beyond r 63.34(3).
#ASSERT `What is the most per hour for this work` `a legal practitioner, doing legal work` 12 TRUE 30 EQUALS JUST 1193.4
#ASSERT `What is the most per hour for this work` `an employee who is not a legal practitioner, doing legal work` 0 TRUE 10 EQUALS JUST 437.8
#ASSERT `What is the most per hour for this work` `a legal practitioner, doing legal work` 12 TRUE 31 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the most per hour for this work` `a legal practitioner, doing legal work` 12 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `What is the most for counsel's fee` `junior counsel` `an appearance day (with that day's conferences, preparation and advice)` TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 7442
#ASSERT `What is the most for counsel's fee` `senior counsel` `an appearance day (with that day's conferences, preparation and advice)` TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 11163
#ASSERT `What is the most for counsel's fee` `junior counsel` `an hour of conferences, preparation or advice on another day` TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 744
#ASSERT `What is the most for counsel's fee` `senior counsel` `an hour of conferences, preparation or advice on another day` TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 1116
-- $11,163 x 1.3 = $14,511.90.
#ASSERT `What is the most for counsel's fee` `senior counsel` `an appearance day (with that day's conferences, preparation and advice)` TRUE 30 EQUALS JUST 14511.9
#ASSERT `What is the most for counsel's fee` `junior counsel` `an appearance day (with that day's conferences, preparation and advice)` FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Order 79 -- money in court`

-- Arguments: for a person under disability, written authority, certified.
#ASSERT `Can the money be paid out without a court order` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the money be paid out without a court order` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the money be paid out without a court order` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the money be paid out without a court order` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Payment Monday 2 November 2026: Monday 9 November. Payment Friday 18 December 2026: 19 to 23 December (5), then 10
-- and 11 January: Monday 11 January 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I be told of the payment into court` (`d` 2 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I be told of the payment into court` (`d` 18 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 11 1 2027

-- $100,000 for 73 days at 10%: 100000 x 0.10 x 73 / 365 = $2000. $250,000 for a year at 10%: $25,000. $50,000 for 30
-- days at 9.5%: 4750 x 30 / 365 = 28500/73 (about $390.41).
#ASSERT `What is the most interest for the delay` TRUE 100000 73 10 EQUALS JUST 2000
#ASSERT `What is the most interest for the delay` TRUE 250000 365 10 EQUALS JUST 25000
#ASSERT `What is the most interest for the delay` TRUE 50000 30 9.5 EQUALS JUST (28500 DIVIDED BY 73)
#ASSERT `What is the most interest for the delay` FALSE 100000 73 10 EQUALS NOTHING

-- A dismissal notified Monday 2 November 2026: one month, Wednesday 2 December. Notified 15 December 2026: 31 days,
-- 16 to 23 December (8), then 10 January to 1 February (23): Monday 1 February 2027. A grant made Monday 2 November:
-- 5 days, weekends out: Monday 9 November; made Thursday 19 November: Thursday 26 November.
#ASSERT `By when may I appeal the payment out order` `the application was dismissed, wholly or in part` (`d` 2 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 2 12 2026
#ASSERT `By when may I appeal the payment out order` `the application was dismissed, wholly or in part` (`d` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 1 2 2027
#ASSERT `By when may I appeal the payment out order` `the application was granted, wholly or in part` (`d` 2 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `By when may I appeal the payment out order` `the application was granted, wholly or in part` (`d` 19 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 26 11 2026

-- Arguments: money held from another court, would be under disability, held in Victoria, lives in Victoria.
#ASSERT `Can money held for me elsewhere be held in this Court` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can money held for me elsewhere be held in this Court` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can money held for me elsewhere be held in this Court` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can money held for me elsewhere be held in this Court` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Order 85 -- child abuse claims against an unincorporated NGO`

#ASSERT `Can I sue the NGO in its own name` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I sue the NGO in its own name` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I sue the NGO in its own name` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 120 plain days: from 2 November 2026, 3 to 30 November (28), December (59), January (90), February (118), 1 and 2 March:
-- 2 March 2027. From 1 January 2027: January (30), February (58), March (89), April (119), 1 May 2027.
#ASSERT `By when may the NGO nominate a proper defendant` (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`d` 2 3 2027)
#ASSERT `By when may the NGO nominate a proper defendant` (`d` 1 1 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`d` 1 5 2027)
#ASSERT `By when may the NGO nominate a proper defendant` (`d` 2 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `By when must the nomination be served on me` (`d` 2 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `By when must the nomination be served on me` (`d` 18 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 11 1 2027

-- Nomination served Monday 2 November 2026: 28 days, Monday 30 November. Served Tuesday 1 December 2026: 2 to 23 December
-- (22), then 10 to 15 January (6): Friday 15 January 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I file my amended writ naming the proper defendant` (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`d` 30 11 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I file my amended writ naming the proper defendant` (`d` 1 12 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`d` 15 1 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I file my amended writ naming the proper defendant` (`d` 2 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: served, directed, done, day done, today.
#ASSERT `Did I file my amended writ in time` (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) (`d` 5 12 2026) EQUALS JUST `taken in time`
#ASSERT `Did I file my amended writ in time` (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 12 2026) (`d` 5 12 2026) EQUALS JUST `not taken in time`
#ASSERT `Did I file my amended writ in time` (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 30 11 2026) EQUALS JUST `still open`
#ASSERT `Did I file my amended writ in time` (`d` 1 12 2026) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 16 1 2027) EQUALS JUST `not taken in time`
#ASSERT `Did I file my amended writ in time` (`d` 2 11 2026) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 30 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
